ref 1069 "q-146208" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527950 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527950 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.45, & y=4 \\\\ 0.55, & y=6 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|8}=5.1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527950 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "611fada0-4ebb-55c6-bcaf-8dccb0c75bca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527950 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)]-{\\mu }_{Y|8}^{2} \\\\  & =[(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.45+(6)^{2}\\cdot 0.55]-(5.1)^{2} \\\\  & =7.2+19.8-26.01 \\\\  & =0.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527963 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527963 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527963 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527963 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{4}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417