iables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527966 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86c9830c-c21b-52dd-a632-55f72d300bd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527966 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+(2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+(4)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}]-(3)^{2} \\\\  & =0+1+10-9 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146246" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|6}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a520314-a8ce-5660-9be7-ab082651f66c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527968 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)]-{\\mu }_{Y|6}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2+8-9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146202" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & x=1 \\\\ 0.6, & x=2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=1.6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f6a4dc1-cc0e-50e8-a876-123c929a6728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527976 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.6]-(1.6)^{2} \\\\  & =0.4+2.4-2.56 \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
